  "parent_protocol": "<local-input>/2394b80cdd99/protocol.json",
  "parent_protocol_sha256": "8c11b322d2c790086594c94feb53533ef425f276202304fa69fb2507a38fefc6",
  "requested_by": " cross-session dispatch (10/6, after host reply \"\" relayed in group messages 20261005T194026Z-14a6, 20261005T195605Z-52ef and 20261005T233526Z-7444): move the closed-loop stress ladder onto the observed-active lane closed loop of scale_A/joint, arm B headline and arm A alongside, zero refits, s = 0 equal to 925/69/12,119.",
  "read_at_that_time": "The nested-scale readings of joint_stress (results.md, summary.json: no crossover, shared margin never looser); scale_A amendment 001 and the lane summaries of scale_A/joint B and A (B loop 925/69/12,119, three-point lane 914/84/12,031, measured-only lane 818/75/13,503; A loop 926/69/12,076, three-point 925/83/11,851, measured-only 822/78/13,443; joint lambdas B 0.08/0.07/0.09/0.04, A 0.10/0.07/0.08/0.04; stage-1 lane 583 and 585 test designs); the test branches, choices and measured four-point effects of scale_A/joint. No corrupted lane rung, no regenerated forecast array and no lane three-point stress value had been computed.",
  "what_changes": {
    "scale": "Plate-own vehicle centres of common_scale R1: arm B (scale from training-associated vehicle controls; headline) and arm A (scale from all unique vehicle controls; alongside). Frozen common_scale R1 outer models, transforms, cutoffs and rank references; the four outer folds and 188 identity groups of the manuscript.",
    "lane": "Stage 1: measured_only >= 3 -> report active; else report the three-point call iff exact m3 > lambda. Otherwise the policy fourth dose (choices already committed, unchanged). Stage 2: measured4 >= 3 -> report active; else report the four-point call iff exact m4 > lambda; else complete. Envelope U_d(lambda) = 0 if measured_only >= 3, else max{e3*1(m3 > lambda), max_c e4c*1(m4c > lambda)*1(measured4c < 3)}, a pointwise upper bound of every policy wrong report under the lane; lambda reselected per arm and fold by the same exact CRC rule. Wells: stage-1 lane charges the three measured concentrations, stage-2 lane adds the fourth-dose wells.",
    "three_point_rule": "anchorboost, measured_only, loglinear: crc_obs of risk_upgrade amendment 004. A design with measured_only >= 3 is released with call active; any other design is released iff its exact margin > lambda; lambda is the first grid value with (sum_g L_g + 1)/(n_cal + 1) <= 1/10 for L_g(lambda) = (1/D_g) * sum over the group designs with measured_only < 3 of 1(margin > lambda) 1(call != truth); exact rational arithmetic.",
    "policies": "The four policies of the parent protocol plus the three classical rules of scale_A/joint (gp_ivr, hill_var, gp_var), whose saved choices do not read the AnchorBoost forecasts and stay fixed. model_disagreement is recomputed per rung from the corrupted three-point channel and the untouched interpolation and training-analog channels.",
    "forecasts": "scale_A/joint scored every branch but saved no forecast array. The forecasts stage regenerates them by inference only: for each arm, fold and role the frozen common_scale R1 outer model on the tasks of run_common.make_tasks with the arm transform, through joint/run_joint.py observed() and forward(), single thread, the code files whose SHA-256 the scale_A prediction freezes record. Channel 0 holds the three-point forecast of every candidate level (meta candidate -1) and the four-point forecast of every remaining level of every candidate branch; channels 1 and 2 hold interpolation and training analog of the three-point rows. Gate: every score3, score4, measured4, disagreement score and the three deterministic choices bit-equal to scale_A records, and the three-point channel bit-equal to the saved common_scale anchorboost forecasts; otherwise the run stops.",
    "noise": "Unchanged definitions of the parent protocol: sigma per arm, fold and output from that arm and fold inner0/inner1 points (anchorboost - truth, masked, ddof = 1); three-point draws numpy default_rng(SeedSequence([20261005, 1, seed, fold, role_code])).standard_normal(shape of the arm three-point forecast array), rows matched by (chemical, design, level); both arms receive the same draws (identical shapes); branch draws stream 3 in branch-row order (independent, primary) or the three-point draw of the same design and level (persistent, secondary); forecast + (s * sigma) * Z.",
    "calibration": "Lane joint envelope per arm and fold: B_d = 0 if measured three points >= 3, else the largest exact block among the wrong three-point call and the wrong calls of branches with measured four points < 3; group numerators by run_start.exact_curve, feasibility by run_start.first_feasible (alpha 1/10). Three-point lane comparator: B_d = block if measured three points < 3 and the call is wrong, else 0, the same exact routines; lane designs count in D_g.",
    "decisions": "Stage 1: lane -> report active; else report call3 iff block3 > lambda index. Stage 2: measured four points >= 3 -> report active; else call4 iff block4 > lambda index; else complete. Three-point lane: lane or block > index.",
    "bootstrap": "The count matrix W of the first default_rng(0).integers(0, 188, (4000, 188)) draw (equal to scale_A/bootstrap_identity_counts_seed0.npz), statistics W @ x as scale_A/joint bootstraps(); at s = 0 it reproduces every scale_A lane interval. One matrix for every arm, rung, variant and rule; the three-point lane comparator gets its single-arm intervals from the same matrix (no published lane three-point ladder exists).",
    "unchanged": "Ladder levels, seeds, alpha, grid, readouts, contrasts, reading rules and the property statement of the parent protocol."
  },
  "gate": {
    "forecasts": "bit-equal reconstruction listed under what_changes.forecasts, per arm, fold and role",
    "s_0": [
      "every per-design row of scale_A/joint/{arm}/lane/design_decisions.csv (7 rules, 2 baselines) reproduced",
      "methods, paired contrasts and identity intervals equal scale_A/joint/{arm}/lane/summary.json exactly",
      "lane joint lambdas equal scale_A (B 0.08/0.07/0.09/0.04; A 0.10/0.07/0.08/0.04); three-point lane lambdas equal headline/lane/three_point_lambdas.json",
      "B model_disagreement 925 reports, 69 wrong, 12,119 wells; A 926/69/12,076; three-point lane B 914/84/12,031, A 925/83/11,851"
    ],
    "lane": "every lane design and lane branch is reference-active (scale_A gate); a violation stops the run"
  },
  "reading": {
    "reading_1": "As the parent reading_1, per arm: D(s, seed) = pooled wells of the lane closed loop (independent, model_disagreement) minus the three-point lane rule under the same rung and seed; crossover = first rung with seed-median D < 0; ties; interpolated crossing between the last positive and first negative rung. Arm B is the headline.",
    "reading_2": "Return to complete measurement: completed / designs by rung, seed medians, ranges, interval medians, monotone check, next to the three-point lane full-measure share.",
    "reading_3": "Wrong-report loss per rung and seed against 0.10, with reports, missed and false activity; lane reports are counted."
  },
  "expected_before_run": {
    "written": "Before any regenerated forecast and any corrupted lane rung. Inputs inspected: scale_A lane summaries and calibration files, and, from frozen test branches, the measured four-point effect of every candidate (no forecast).",
    "s_0": {
      "B": "loop 925/69/12,119 (43.16%), completed 40 (4.15%), loss 7.18% [5.05%, 9.47%]; three-point lane 914/84/12,031 (42.85%), D = +88",
      "A": "loop 926/69/12,076; three-point lane 925/83/11,851, D = +225"
    },
    "s_ge_4": {
      "mechanism": "Corruption cannot touch the lanes. At s >= 4 no non-lane design clears the margin in either arm, so the three-point lane rule reports exactly its lane designs and the loop adds every non-lane design whose policy fourth dose reaches the activity line.",
      "three_point": {
        "B": "583 reports, 17,653 wells (62.87%), return rate 39.59%",
        "A": "585 reports, 17,605 wells (62.70%)"
      },
      "loop": {
        "B": "disagreement picks follow the noise, so stage-2 lanes near the uniform-random level of 65.6: wells about 16,849 (60.0%), D about -805 (planning range -1,505 to -500), return rate about 32.8% (26%-36%); with frozen choices highest_unmeasured -1,619, fixed_maximin -1,179, gp_ivr -994, hill_var -1,198, gp_var -1,224",
        "A": "uniform-random level 66.4 stage-2 lanes, D about -809; highest_unmeasured -1,619"
      },
      "loss": "0 in both arms: only lane reports remain and lane reports are reference-active"
    },
    "s_le_2": "D > 0 at s <= 1 (the lane joint margin is never looser than the three-point lane margin, as on the nested scale); the sign at s = 2 is open: stage-2 lanes repay part of the stricter margin.",
    "crossover": "Between s = 2 and s = 4 for both arms (interpolated), possibly already at s = 2; this matches the dispatch expectation s = 2-3 that the nested scale did not meet.",
    "wrong_loss": "Medians <= 0.10 on every rung and at or below the three-point lane medians at s <= 2; 0 at s >= 4.",
    "persistent": "Smaller D than independent at every rung with reports, crossover no later than independent.",
    "interpretation": "Planning ranges, not acceptance criteria. Readouts outside them are reported as they are."
  },
